    "thesis": "Round 48 cell on the taxable trading book: base `i13f` (`I-13f-duquesne-2026q2`, the card seated on `app.paperdesk.desk.AGENT_IDS` today), read verbatim from `backend/app/paper/library/candidates/I-13f-duquesne-2026q2.json` -- entry 'close > sma(50) and close > sma(200) and rsi(14) > 50', exit 'close crosses_below sma(50)', stop 0.12, take-profit None, hold cap 120, 6 slots at 0.15 each. This base carries 13F point-in-time provenance: its universe was not knowable before 2026-08-14 (the filing date), so it is expected UNRANKED on every main window that starts before that date -- reported, not interpreted, per PROTOCOL.md section 5 and section 9's r2 amendment. Arm `risk1pct`, round 45's follow-up question asked of every seated trading card: position size becomes Decimal('0.01') / this base's stop_loss_pct, quantised to 3dp (0.083 here, since every base in this round carries a 0.12 stop) -- slot count and every other field unchanged. Round 45 measured this exact resizing lower the tail (worst window, IQR) and mean exposure on Creator E's own card without moving the per-window sign pattern, at a cost to the median. Predicted here to repeat that shape on the four other bases, and to be near-inert on the fifth if its own position size barely moves relative to its stop. Pre-registered 2026-09-09, before any measurement (see strategy-program/ROUND-48-PLAN.md). Nothing here is promotable -- the `trading` purpose is exempt from PROTOCOL.md section 6 promotion (r21 amendment); this is a measurement study, report only, and a decision to resize a seated card for real is the owner's, about risk, not this round's to make. Not investment advice.",
